- providers go offline
- APIs timeout
- webhooks arrive late
- webhooks arrive twice
- webhooks arrive out of order
- provider state conflicts with Enigma state
- CDRs arrive hours later
- tariffs change
- sessions disappear
- refunds partially succeed
- payment providers fail
- networks partition
- databases fail over
- messages are duplicated
- clients retry aggressively

Implement:

- idempotency
- retry policies
- exponential backoff
- jitter
- circuit breakers where appropriate
- timeout budgets
- dead-letter queues
- replay mechanisms
- compensating transactions
- reconciliation jobs
- operational runbooks
- graceful degradation
- kill switches
- provider isolation
- backpressure
- rate limiting

Do not blindly retry financial or physical-world commands.

Every command must have a safety classification.

